This repository contains Palomar-ready Lean 4 projects (Lean v4.36.0, Mathlib fc4f59e) of proofs that
Ming-Chih Kao (GitHub: koolkao) submitted to Left to Solve
(https://github.com/GuillaumeBAUD-coder/open-math-agents) and that were merged there, and of results first
published in his own public repositories (github.com/koolkao/mo505921-tanh-dominance,
friedan-entropy-inequality, feige-lean, gillibert-equal-halves-counterexample,
kimberling-copula-inequality, mo451543-jensen-slack, mo478827-binomial-monotone,
mo184460-hellinger-tv, mo503314-two-primes). The merged Left to Solve files themselves are archived in the companion
repository left-to-solve-proofs. Ming-Chih Kao licenses his contributions under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.

formal-conjectures
------------------
The problem statements and the definitions they use come from formal-conjectures
(https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures, commit
9097e2f90e66d2f6244209cb1c07f7120d17ec53), Copyright 2025 and 2026 The Formal Conjectures Authors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. They are adapted (with the original copyright lines and
a statement of the changes) in palomar/*/Challenge.lean and palomar/*/*/Defs.lean. Two short lemmas
copied from the same files (lebesgueFunction_eq, localTime_le_maxLocalTime) are marked in the files that contain them.

Hadamard sequence data
----------------------
The sequence data in palomar/hadamard-first-cases/ were regenerated from published tables: the numbers
were extracted from the tables compiled in SageMath (https://www.sagemath.org, GPL-2.0-or-later) and
re-encoded as Lean data. No SageMath code is included. The papers the numbers come from are cited in
the proof file.

