MathlibExt/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/KyFan.lean from facebookresearch/atlas-lean (commit
44517525f25d2f7ce7a99e1bce7567d9583c9c4f), Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates, licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0; the changes are listed in its header, and the upstream licence file
(FriedanQ/Vendor/LICENSE-atlas-lean) is copied verbatim, including its first line: "Codebase is not intended
for use to train, fine-tune, distill, evaluate, or otherwise develop ML models". The proof depends on physlib
(https://github.com/leanprover-community/physlib, commit edc607c2e6cbcc2f9c40c750e5c10a8490d32470,
Apache-2.0) as a pinned Lake dependency; its licence is copied as FriedanQ/Vendor/LICENSE-physlib.

TauCeti (palomar/kimberling-copula)
-----------------------------------
palomar/kimberling-copula/KimberlingCopula/TauCeti.lean contains Bernstein's theorem on [0, ∞) and its
dependency closure from TauCeti (https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti, commit ac8801f6), Copyright (c)
2026 The Tau Ceti contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, adapted to Mathlib fc4f59e
(see the header of the file).

Holt–Royle census (palomar/gillibert-equal-halves)
--------------------------------------------------
The adjacency lists in palomar/gillibert-equal-halves/EqualHalves/Proof.lean encode graphs of the census of
vertex-transitive graphs by D. Holt and G. Royle (doi:10.5281/zenodo.4010122), licensed under Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0.

scripts/check-lean-sources.py follows PalomarRegistry/PalomarTemplate's script of the same name
(Apache-2.0).
